1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Electing a populist mayor blows up local debt — but why does it happen?

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Data on 8,000 Italian municipalities reveal the mechanism. The problem is not ideology,

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
but the duty to keep impossible promises.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Picture a town hall. The new mayor insists on funding right away

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
the pledges from his campaign, completely ignoring the town's economic reality.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
That is when the block kicks in.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Technical managers look at the budget and freeze spending.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Unable to admit the mistake to voters, the mayor removes the obstacle.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
He forces out experienced technicians and replaces them with less skilled but obedient staff.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Without expertise as a filter, the administrative machine derails.

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The ability to repay debt collapses and contract costs skyrocket.

12
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
So, to parade the completion of a single campaign slogan,

13
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:59,000
the administration burns its best talent and leaves citizens with a hefty bill.
